[claude:event result] {"duration_api_ms":13927,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7d8463e0-da60-4a40-a0f3-600be7853b61","total_cost_usd":0.0094406,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":12921,"output_tokens":1207,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":456},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":9,"output_tokens":1207,"cache_read_input_tokens":12921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":802,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1017,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001102,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-4-5":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":1207,"cacheReadInputTokens":12921,"cacheCreationInputTokens":802,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0083386,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":456,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a webserver. This involves creating a bare git repository with a post-receive hook that deploys to the web directory.\n\nHere's what you need to do on the server:\n\n**1. Create the bare git repository:**\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n**2. Create a post-receive hook** that deploys changes to the webserver:\n```bash\nsudo tee /git/server/hooks/post-receive > /dev/null <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\n\nWORK_DIR=\"/tmp/git-deploy\"\nWEB_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\n\n# Clone/update working copy\nif [ ! -d \"$WORK_DIR\" ]; then\n    git clone /git/server \"$WORK_DIR\"\nelse\n    cd \"$WORK_DIR\"\n    git pull\nfi\n\n# Copy files to webserver\ncp -r \"$WORK_DIR\"/* \"$WEB_DIR\"/ 2>/dev/null || true\n\necho \"Deployed to $WEB_DIR\"\nEOF\n\nsudo chmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\nsudo chown git:git -R /git/server  # or whatever user runs git\n```\n\n**3. Set up the webserver on port 8080:**\n\n**Option A: Using Python (simplest)**\n```bash\nsudo tee /etc/systemd/system/webserver.service > /dev/null <<'EOF'\n[Unit]\nDescription=Simple Web Server on Port 8080\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nType=simple\nWorkingDirectory=/var/www/html\nExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 -m http.server 8080\nRestart=on-failure\nUser=www-data\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\nEOF\n\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/html\nsudo systemctl daemon-reload\nsudo systemctl enable webserver\nsudo systemctl start webserver\n```\n\n**Option B: Using nginx**\n```bash\nsudo apt-get install nginx\n\nsudo tee /etc/nginx/sites-available/default > /dev/null <<'EOF'\nserver {\n    listen 8080;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n}\nEOF\n\nsudo systemctl restart nginx\n```\n\n**4. Fix permissions** so the git hook can write to the web directory:\n```bash\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/html\nsudo chown www-data:www-data /var/www/html\nsudo chmod 755 /var/www/html\n```\n\nThen from your local machine:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\ncd server\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n```\n\nThe post-receive hook will automatically run after each push and deploy your files to `/var/www/html`, making them accessible via HTTP on port 8080.\n\nWhat OS is your server running? I can refine these commands if needed.","ttft_ms":6142,"type":"result","duration_ms":12837,"uuid":"dd3c9561-e9af-4926-9f87-787006f14534","ttft_stream_ms":998,"time_to_request_ms":83,"queued_turn_count":0}
